wer.type/math "9"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040608/state.json" "file_sha256" "b5dc5188d8fdf6aafffa23f9aa3023e6b5623ad9e1db3086f8368ea1909ef020" "basis" 1451 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040608/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97422" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $V={R}_{2}[t]$ be the vector space of all polynomials of degree at most $2,$ equipped with the inner product\n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩=x(1)y(1)+x(0)y(0)+x(-1)y(-1).\n$$\n\nCalculate the norm of the vector $p(t)=4-{t}^{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040608/state.json" "file_sha256" "b5dc5188d8fdf6aafffa23f9aa3023e6b5623ad9e1db3086f8368ea1909ef020" "basis" 1451 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040608/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97422" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The norm of a vector $p(t)$ with respect to an inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖p(t)‖=\\sqrt{⟨p(t),p(t)⟩}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $p(t)=4-{t}^{2},$ we obtain\n\n$$\np(1)=3,\\,p(0)=4,\\,p(-1)=3.\n$$\n\nComputing $‖p(t)‖$ using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖p(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{⟨p(t),p(t)⟩} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{p(1)p(1)+p(0)p(0)+p(-1)p(-1)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{[p(1)]^{2}+[p(0)]^{2}+[p(-1)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(3)^{2}+(4)^{2}+(3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+16+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{34}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040608/state.json" "file_sha256" "b5dc5188d8fdf6aafffa23f9aa3023e6b5623ad9e1db3086f8368ea1909ef020" "basis" 1451 "verification" "/home/ja