3}}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040608/state.json" "file_sha256" "b5dc5188d8fdf6aafffa23f9aa3023e6b5623ad9e1db3086f8368ea1909ef020" "basis" 1451 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040608/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-141170" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040608/state.json" "file_sha256" "b5dc5188d8fdf6aafffa23f9aa3023e6b5623ad9e1db3086f8368ea1909ef020" "basis" 1451 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040608/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97726" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "An inner product on $V={R}^{3}$ is defined as $⟨x,y⟩=2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+{x}_{3}{y}_{3}.$ \n\nNormalize the  vector $v=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]$ under this inner product." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040608/state.json" "file_sha256" "b5dc5188d8fdf6aafffa23f9aa3023e6b5623ad9e1db3086f8368ea1909ef020" "basis" 1451 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040608/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97726" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The norm of a vector $v$ with respect to an inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖v‖=\\sqrt{⟨v,v⟩}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨v,v⟩ & =2\\cdot (3\\cdot 3)+2\\cdot (2\\cdot 2)+(-3)\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =18+8+9 \\\\  & =35.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖v‖ & =\\sqrt{35}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo normalize the vector $v$, we divide $v$ by its norm $‖v‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{v}{‖v‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{35}}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{35}}{35}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040608/state.json" "file_sha256" "b5dc5188d8fdf6aafffa23f9aa3023e6b5623ad9e1db3086f8368ea1909ef020" "basis" 1451 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040608/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97726" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040608/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6b3dde96a478b61d719fd518dcbfe870937305ab4a3d5e1e2ed43ec4aebbdce6" "basis" 1451 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040608/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97726" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040608/state.json" "file_sha256" "b5dc5188d8fdf6aafffa23f9aa3023e6b5623ad9e1db3086f8368ea1909ef020" "basis" 1451 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040608/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97726" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{22}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Deve